-      "spec": "Implement shipping method metadata denormalization for orders and expose it correctly via GraphQL.\n\n1) Copy shipping method metadata for all delivery methods during checkout-to-order conversion:\n- File: saleor/checkout/complete_checkout.py\n- Function: _process_shipping_data_for_order\n- Change: Always include shipping method metadata in the returned result when the delivery method is a ShippingMethodData instance. Remove the is_external condition. Specifically, when isinstance(shipping_method, ShippingMethodData), update result with both \"shipping_method_metadata\": shipping_method.metadata and \"shipping_method_private_metadata\": shipping_method.private_metadata.\n\n2) Denormalize shipping method metadata during draft order completion:\n- File: saleor/graphql/order/mutations/draft_order_complete.py\n- Location: In DraftOrderComplete.perform_mutation, just before computing the search vector and saving the order.\n- Logic: If order.shipping_method is set, copy its metadata and private_metadata into the order:\n  - order.shipping_method_metadata = order.shipping_method.metadata\n  - order.shipping_method_private_metadata = order.shipping_method.private_metadata\n  - Add both fields (\"shipping_method_metadata\", \"shipping_method_private_metadata\") to update_fields so they are persisted on order.save(update_fields=update_fields).\n\n3) Expose denormalized shipping method metadata via GraphQL Order type for built-in shipping methods:\n- File: saleor/graphql/order/types.py\n- Resolver: Order.resolve_shipping_method (the internal/built-in shipping method path)\n- After building shipping_method_data = convert_to_shipping_method_data(shipping_method, listing, tax_class), apply:\n  - If order.status == OrderStatus.DRAFT: return shipping_method_data as-is.\n  - Else (non-draft):\n    - If order.shipping_method_metadata is not None, set shipping_method_data.metadata = order.shipping_method_metadata\n    - If order.shipping_method_private_metadata is not None, set shipping_method_data.private_metadata = order.shipping_method_private_metadata\n  - Return shipping_method_data\n- Note: Keep external shipping method path unchanged (it already uses order’s metadata fields).\n\nBehavioral expectations:\n- Orders created from checkout must contain shipping_method_metadata for both external and built-in shipping methods.\n- Draft order completion must persist shipping method metadata into the order.\n- For draft orders, GraphQL shows the current ShippingMethod’s metadata; for non-draft orders, it shows the denormalized order metadata when present, falling back to the ShippingMethod’s metadata for older orders.\n\nThis aligns with the new tests added in the diff and existing behavior for external shipping methods.",
-      "prompt": "Update the order creation flow so that shipping method metadata is denormalized onto the order in all cases, and update GraphQL to expose it consistently.\n\nSpecifically:\n- When completing checkout, always copy the selected shipping method’s public and private metadata into the order, regardless of whether the method is external or built-in.\n- When finalizing a draft order, copy the selected shipping method’s public and private metadata into the order before saving.\n- In the GraphQL order type, when resolving the shipping method for built-in methods: for draft orders return the shipping method’s current metadata; for non-draft orders return the metadata stored on the order if available, falling back to the shipping method’s metadata for older orders.\n\nDo not modify tests; implement the behavior so existing and new tests for shipping method metadata denormalization and exposure pass.",
