-      "id": "add-discount-expiration",
-      "sha": "261bbc8d35c40c4e5b3078c25418724d1a35c7a2",
-      "parentSha": "95dbffbc523a5a8865ead2a2649913491ac8e89c",
-      "spec": "Implement discount expiration tracking and targeted checkout discount recalculation, and fix gift line updates when promotions change.\n\nScope\n- Introduce a dedicated discount expiration on Checkout and integrate it across recalculation, invalidation, and persistence paths.\n- Rework discount creation utilities to return the soonest promotion end date and use it to cap the discount expiration.\n- Adjust gift reward handling to always produce a fresh line info object and avoid negative unit price issues when gifts change.\n- Update GraphQL checkout lines resolver to recalculate discounts (only) when needed, using lines info and checkout info dataloaders.\n- Ensure all existing price expiration touchpoints also update discount expiration.\n- Update and add tests (unit, benchmark, e2e) to cover the new behavior.\n\nRequirements\n1) Data model and migrations\n- Add a new field to saleor/checkout/models.py on Checkout:\n  - discount_expiration: DateTimeField with default timezone.now.\n  - Include a comment that it controls when discounts should be refreshed and whether to update discounts prior to tax recalculation.\n- Create a Django migration to add discount_expiration to checkout_checkout with a DB default of NOW(). Include reverse SQL to drop the default. Add merge migrations as needed to resolve existing migration branches.\n\n2) Checkout calculation flow\n- In saleor/checkout/calculations.py:\n  - Implement a new function recalculate_discounts(checkout_info, lines_info, database_connection_name=..., force_update=False) that:\n    - Checks stale conditions: If not force_update and either checkout.discount_expiration > now OR checkout.price_expiration > now, skip recalculation and return.\n    - Cast lines_info to a list and call update_undiscounted_unit_price_for_lines and update_prior_unit_price_for_lines.\n    - Call create_or_update_discount_objects_from_promotion_for_checkout and capture the soonest applied promotion end date (may be None).\n    - Set checkout.discount_expiration to the minimum of soonest promotion end date and (now + settings.CHECKOUT_PRICES_TTL) when available; else set it to (now + settings.CHECKOUT_PRICES_TTL).\n    - Save checkout with update_fields=[\"discount_expiration\"] using the default DB connection.\n    - Return the potentially updated checkout_info and lines.\n  - In _fetch_checkout_prices_if_expired, replace the direct discount update path with recalculate_discounts(checkout_info, lines, database_connection_name=..., force_update=force_update).\n  - When the overall price refresh completes, set both checkout.price_expiration and checkout.discount_expiration to the same computed expiration (now + CHECKOUT_PRICES_TTL). Include discount_expiration in the fields saved and in any update_fields lists.\n\n3) Invalidation and utility updates\n- In saleor/checkout/utils.py:\n  - invalidate_checkout_prices: when marking checkout for recalculation, set both price_expiration and discount_expiration to timezone.now(). The function should return updated_fields that include [\"price_expiration\", \"discount_expiration\", \"last_change\"]. When save=True, persist both.\n  - add_variant_to_checkout: when invalidating prices after adding/updating a line, set both price_expiration and discount_expiration to timezone.now().\n\n4) Discount utilities\n- In saleor/discount/utils/checkout.py:\n  - create_or_update_discount_objects_from_promotion_for_checkout should return the soonest end date across catalogue and order promotions, if any.\n  - create_checkout_line_discount_objects_for_catalogue_promotions should return a datetime | None representing the soonest end date of applied catalogue promotions for the current lines. It should forward the soonest_end_date computed by prepare_checkout_line_discount_objects_for_catalogue_promotions.\n  - prepare_checkout_line_discount_objects_for_catalogue_promotions should collect end_date from each applied promotion rule (if present) and return the soonest_end_date as an additional element of the tuple output alongside the existing create/update/remove lists and updated_fields. When no dates are present, return None.\n  - create_checkout_discount_objects_for_order_promotions should return the promotion end date or None. If a voucher is set, clear checkout-level discounts and return None. If neither gift nor discount object is created, clear checkout-level discounts and return None.\n- In saleor/discount/utils/promotion.py:\n  - Change create_discount_objects_for_order_promotions to return a 3-tuple: (gift_promotion_applied, discount_object, promotion_end_date). Set promotion_end_date to the selected rule's promotion.end_date (or None).\n  - Update create_gift_line signature to return only the created/updated line (remove boolean created flag); adjust all callers accordingly.\n  - In _handle_gift_reward, after creating or updating the gift line and its discount:\n    - Replace any existing line info for this line with a freshly constructed CheckoutLineInfo or EditableOrderLineInfo including the new discount and rules_info. Append this updated line info to the lines_info list. This ensures line-discount consistency and prevents negative unit price when the gift reward changes.\n\n5) GraphQL resolver changes\n- In saleor/graphql/checkout/types.py:\n  - Add a helper get_dataloaders_for_recalculate_discounts(root, info) that returns promises for lines info and checkout info by token using CheckoutLinesInfoByCheckoutTokenLoader and CheckoutInfoByCheckoutTokenLoader.\n  - In Checkout.resolve_lines:\n    - Use Promise.all over these two dataloaders, and in the callback (wrapped with allow_writer_in_context):\n      - Call calculations.recalculate_discounts(checkout_info, lines_info, database_connection_name) where database_connection_name is obtained from the current context.\n      - Return a list/tuple of SyncWebhookControlContext objects wrapping each line_info.line with the existing allow_sync_webhooks flag.\n    - Remove direct use of CheckoutLinesByCheckoutTokenLoader; lines should be obtained as lines info so discount recalculation can mutate gift lines when necessary.\n\n6) Other update points\n- In saleor/graphql/tax/mutations/tax_exemption_manage.py, when handling Checkout, include discount_expiration in update_fields in addition to tax_exemption, price_expiration, last_change, and ensure invalidation method sets both expirations.\n- In saleor/shipping/tasks.py, when clearing invalid shipping methods from checkouts, update fields with shipping_method=None, price_expiration=now, discount_expiration=now, last_change=now using a single captured current_time.\n\n7) Tests\n- Update existing tests that persist price_expiration to also set and assert discount_expiration and include it in update_fields.\n- Update GraphQL checkout lines resolver-dependent tests and bench tests to account for one extra query where applicable (increment expected queries accordingly in benchmark tests).\n- Add a new test module saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/test_checkout_discount_expiration.py that covers:\n  - Querying basic checkout fields does not trigger any recalculation and leaves both expirations unchanged.\n  - Querying only line IDs triggers discount recalculation (when expired) and updates gift lines without recalculating taxes; discount_expiration is capped to the soonest promotion end date when earlier than TTL.\n  - Querying line prices triggers both discount and tax recalculation; both expirations are updated and equal; gift line pricing is zero while undiscounted values are positive.\n  - Cases for gift promotion removal and addition for both ID-only and price queries as above.\n  - Parametrized cases where price_expiration and/or discount_expiration are in the future; no recalculation occurs and gift lines are not changed.\n- Update e2e flow in saleor/tests/e2e/checkout/test_checkout_with_gift_promotion_updates.py to verify:\n  - Gift line is added when promotion becomes active upon delivery method update.\n  - Gift line remains unchanged if expiration is in future.\n  - Gift line updates to a new variant upon a subsequent cart change that invalidates prices/discounts.\n  - Checkout completes successfully and the order contains the correct gift line with zero price.\n- Adjust e2e GraphQL snippets that read checkout/order lines to include isGift and needed fields and reflect any field ordering changes used by assertions.\n- Minor test fix in saleor/graphql/order/tests/queries/test_order_with_where.py to use a different number in an eq filter to avoid accidental matches.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- A checkout with expired discount_expiration but valid price_expiration will recalculate discounts (including gift lines) without calculating taxes.\n- A checkout with expired price_expiration (or both expired) will fully recalculate prices and taxes and set both expirations to the same value (now + TTL).\n- When a gift promotion changes or is removed/added, the gift line in the checkout updates accordingly and never shows a negative unit price. Undiscounted values reflect the original price.\n- All modified save/update_fields include discount_expiration alongside price_expiration as specified.\n- All tests (unit, benchmark, e2e) pass with updated expectations.",
