-      "spec": "Implement variant double-write for variant attribute value assignments and adjust related migrations, utils, and tests.\n\n1) Model update\n- File: saleor/attribute/models/product_variant.py\n  - Extend AssignedVariantAttributeValue with a new nullable ForeignKey field:\n    - name: variant\n    - to: product.ProductVariant\n    - on_delete: models.CASCADE\n    - related_name: \"attributevalues\"\n    - null=True, blank=True\n  - Keep existing Meta unique_together ((\"value\", \"assignment\")) and ordering.\n\n2) Utils refactor and double-write\n- File: saleor/attribute/utils.py\n  - Imports:\n    - Add: from django.conf import settings\n    - Remove: functools.reduce import; remove unused AttributePage and AttributeProduct imports.\n  - instance_to_function_variables_mapping:\n    - Change to tuples of (value_model, instance_field_name) instead of (instance_attribute_model, value_model, instance_field_name):\n      - \"Product\": (AssignedProductAttributeValue, \"product\")\n      - \"ProductVariant\": (AssignedVariantAttributeValue, \"variant\")\n      - \"Page\": (AssignedPageAttributeValue, \"page\")\n  - validate_attribute_owns_values:\n    - If attr_val_map is empty, return.\n    - Build the Q lookup by iterating over attr_val_map and OR-ing Q(attribute_id=<id>, slug__in=[v.slug ...]).\n    - Fetch with replica: AttributeValue.objects.using(settings.DATABASE_CONNECTION_REPLICA_NAME).filter(lookup).\n    - Validate exact slug match per attribute; raise AssertionError otherwise.\n    - Rewrite attr_val_map values in-place to the fetched AttributeValue instances (with ids).\n  - _associate_attribute_to_instance:\n    - Adjust unpacking from mapping to (value_model, instance_field_name).\n    - For ProductVariant instances:\n      - Compute instance_attrs_ids with AttributeVariant.objects.filter(attribute_id__in=attr_val_map.keys(), product_type_id=instance.product.product_type_id).values_list(\"pk\", flat=True).\n      - Use _get_or_create_assignments(instance, instance_attrs_ids, AssignedVariantAttribute, instance_field_name) to get assignments.\n    - Call _overwrite_values(..., None if instance_field_name == \"variant\" else instance_field_name).\n    - For variants, call the updated _order_variant_assigned_attr_values(values_order_map, assignments, attr_val_map). For others, call _order_assigned_attr_values as before.\n  - _order_variant_assigned_attr_values signature and behavior:\n    - Signature: _order_variant_assigned_attr_values(values_order_map, assignments, attr_val_map)\n    - Query AssignedVariantAttributeValue.objects.filter(assignment_id__in=[a.pk ...], value_id__in=[v.pk ...]).\n    - For each row, set sort_order = values_order_map[value.assignment_id].index(value.value_id).\n    - Double-write variant: set value.variant_id = value.assignment.variant_id.\n    - bulk_update(assigned_attrs_values, [\"sort_order\", \"variant\"]) to persist both fields.\n\n3) Data migrations\n- File: saleor/attribute/migrations/0034_assignedpageattributevalue_page_data_migration.py\n  - In update_page_assignment() CTE selecting rows to update, change ordering for the locked batch:\n    - FROM: ORDER BY av.id DESC\n    - TO:   ORDER BY av.sort_order, av.id DESC\n- File: saleor/attribute/migrations/0036_assignedproductattributevalue_product_data_migration.py\n  - In the subquery selecting ids to update, change ordering:\n    - FROM: ORDER BY ID DESC\n    - TO:   ORDER BY SORT_ORDER, ID DESC\n- New file: saleor/attribute/migrations/0055_assignedvariantattributevalue_variant.py\n  - Dependencies:\n    - (\"product\", \"0197_productvariantchannellisting_prior_price_amount\")\n    - (\"attribute\", \"0054_attribute_reference_page_and_product_types\")\n  - Operations:\n    - migrations.AddField on model \"assignedvariantattributevalue\": add the nullable ForeignKey \"variant\" to product.ProductVariant with related_name=\"attributevalues\" and on_delete=CASCADE.\n    - migrations.RunPython: data_migration that, in a loop, updates attribute_assignedvariantattributevalue.variant_id to the variant_id from attribute_assignedvariantattribute by matching assignment_id. Perform updates in batches (BATCH_SIZE=500) using a transaction; select rows WHERE VARIANT_ID IS NULL ORDER BY SORT_ORDER, ID DESC LIMIT %s FOR UPDATE; repeat until none remain.\n\n4) Tests\n- File: saleor/attribute/tests/test_utils.py\n  - Remove attribute_1 and attribute_2 fixtures.\n  - Inline creation of two attributes and one value each inside test_validate_attribute_owns_values; update assertions to compare the concrete value objects created in the test.\n  - Add test_associate_attribute_to_variant_copies_data_over_to_new_field:\n    - Using variant and attribute_value_generator fixtures, create a second value for the variant’s attribute.\n    - Call associate_attribute_values_to_instance(variant, {attribute.id: values}).\n    - Assert variant.attributevalues.count() == 2.\n    - Assert list(variant.attributevalues.values_list(\"value_id\", \"variant_id\")) == [(values[0].pk, variant.id), (values[1].pk, variant.id)].\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- AssignedVariantAttributeValue has a nullable variant FK with related_name=\"attributevalues\".\n- Associating attribute values to a variant results in AssignedVariantAttributeValue rows with correct sort_order and non-null variant_id matching the variant.\n- validate_attribute_owns_values uses the replica connection and rewrites attr_val_map values to DB-fetched AttributeValue instances.\n- Migrations 0034 and 0036 now order batches by sort_order then id before FOR UPDATE.\n- New migration 0055 backfills variant_id in batches, using proper locking; it is idempotent.\n- Updated tests pass, including the new variant double-write test and the refactored attribute ownership validation test.",
-      "prompt": "Extend variant attribute value assignments to store a direct reference to the variant and keep it in sync. Add a nullable variant foreign key to the variant attribute value model and ensure that any time attribute values are associated with a variant, those rows also store the variant id. Include a robust data migration that backfills existing rows in batches with proper locking and ordering. Update the validation logic to read AttributeValue from the read replica. Adjust two prior data migrations to select batches ordered by sort order then id for stability. Update tests to inline simple attribute fixtures and to verify that assigning values to a variant double-writes the variant id onto the value rows.",
