-      "id": "optimize-graphql-metrics",
-      "sha": "5c728c13cab6373088525a2a5462c01d0f0c4c66",
-      "parentSha": "45331bfa801de4f08a05347eeefd7826ba8c753c",
-      "spec": "Implement GraphQL metrics optimization and supporting utilities:\n\n1) Add slow GraphQL operation metric and refactor duration recording\n- File: saleor/graphql/metrics.py\n  - Define a new histogram metric named \"saleor.graphql.slow_operation.duration\" with:\n    - scope: Scope.CORE\n    - type: MetricType.HISTOGRAM\n    - unit: Unit.SECOND\n    - description: \"Duration of slow GraphQL operations.\"\n    - bucket_boundaries: DEFAULT_DURATION_BUCKETS\n  - Replace record_graphql_query_duration with a contextmanager that:\n    - Yields a dict[str, AttributeValue] to be populated by the caller.\n    - Measures duration with a monotonic clock.\n    - On exit, if duration >= settings.TELEMETRY_SLOW_GRAPHQL_OPERATION_THRESHOLD:\n      - Records to the slow-operation duration metric, including any attributes present (the operation fingerprint may be included here).\n    - Removes the graphql.document_fingerprint attribute from the attributes dict before recording the regular duration metric.\n    - Records the duration to \"saleor.graphql.operation.duration\" with unit Unit.SECOND and attributes (without fingerprint).\n- Ensure the existing METRIC_GRAPHQL_QUERY_DURATION still uses DEFAULT_DURATION_BUCKETS.\n\n2) Simplify GraphQL count and cost metric attributes\n- File: saleor/graphql/metrics.py\n  - Update record_graphql_query_count signature to only accept:\n    - amount: int = 1\n    - keyword-only: operation_type: str | None = \"\"\n    - error_type: str | None = None\n  - Record attributes only for graphql.operation.type and error.type (if provided). Do not include graphql.operation.identifier or operation_name.\n  - Update record_graphql_query_cost similarly: accept only cost: int, keyword-only operation_type and error_type; record the same attributes set (no identifier; no operation name).\n\n3) Update GraphQL view to populate/follow new metric attributes and duration flow\n- File: saleor/graphql/views.py\n  - When extracting identifiers, continue setting tracing span attributes for:\n    - saleor_attributes.GRAPHQL_OPERATION_IDENTIFIER\n    - saleor_attributes.GRAPHQL_DOCUMENT_FINGERPRINT\n  - For the query_duration_attrs (the dict yielded by record_graphql_query_duration):\n    - Stop setting saleor_attributes.GRAPHQL_OPERATION_IDENTIFIER.\n    - Set saleor_attributes.GRAPHQL_DOCUMENT_FINGERPRINT instead so that it can be used by the slow-operation metric.\n  - Update all calls to record_graphql_query_count and record_graphql_query_cost to match the new signatures and attribute behavior (pass only operation_type and optional error_type; do not pass operation_name or operation_identifier).\n\n4) Add a configurable threshold for slow GraphQL operations\n- File: saleor/settings.py\n  - Add TELEMETRY_SLOW_GRAPHQL_OPERATION_THRESHOLD, defaulting to 1.0 seconds, configurable via env var of the same name, with a comment describing its purpose.\n\n5) Enhance metrics test utilities with scope-aware helpers\n- File: saleor/tests/utils.py\n  - Modify get_metric_data to accept a keyword-only scope: Scope (default Scope.SERVICE). Return the first Metric matching metric_name within the specified scope of the only resource; return None if not found; fail the test if more than one resource is present.\n  - Add get_metric_and_data_point(metrics_data, metric_name, *, scope=Scope.SERVICE) -> tuple[Metric, DataPointT] which:\n    - Fails the test if the metric is not found or has zero or multiple data points.\n  - Update get_metric_data_point to accept scope and forward to the new helper.\n\n6) Update core telemetry test for histogram bucket boundaries\n- File: saleor/core/telemetry/tests/test_metric.py\n  - Update test_meter_create_histogram_with_explicit_bucket_boundaries to fetch the metric with scope=Scope.CORE via get_metric_data(..., scope=Scope.CORE).\n\n7) Refactor GraphQL metrics tests to use in-memory metrics and verify new behavior\n- File: saleor/graphql/tests/test_metrics.py\n  - Replace meter mocks with assertions against the in-memory metrics data via the get_test_metrics_data fixture and the new helpers (get_metric_and_data_point, get_metric_data).\n  - Validate that:\n    - Count metric records attributes only for graphql.operation.type and optional error.type.\n    - Cost metric uses histogram buckets QUERY_COST_BUCKETS and records only graphql.operation.type and optional error.type.\n    - Duration metric uses DEFAULT_DURATION_BUCKETS, Unit.SECOND, does not include graphql.document_fingerprint, and records one data point per request.\n    - Slow-operation duration metric is recorded only when duration >= TELEMETRY_SLOW_GRAPHQL_OPERATION_THRESHOLD, and includes graphql.document_fingerprint in its attributes.\n  - Add tests that freeze time to simulate durations below and at/above the slow threshold and assert the presence/absence of the slow-operation metric accordingly.\n  - In HTTP-level request metrics tests, assert count and duration metrics via helpers and do not rely on mocks.\n\nBehavioral outcomes to verify:\n- saleor.graphql.operation.count and saleor.graphql.operation.cost no longer include graphql.operation.identifier nor operation name in attributes.\n- saleor.graphql.operation.duration always recorded; attributes do not contain graphql.document_fingerprint.\n- saleor.graphql.slow_operation.duration recorded only for slow queries and includes graphql.document_fingerprint.\n- TELEMETRY_SLOW_GRAPHQL_OPERATION_THRESHOLD controls slow-operation recording.\n- Test utilities support scope filtering and provide helpful failure messages.",
