-      "id": "filter-collection-references",
-      "sha": "f72733245dd939ef700f8d915c381d60f12a0c1c",
-      "parentSha": "b0fa12bd24500100c59df404e5a46833711d6a13",
-      "spec": "Implement filtering by Collection references for attribute-based filters across pages, products, and product variants. Make consistent changes across GraphQL inputs, shared helpers, filters, and tests.\n\nScope and requirements:\n1) GraphQL input support for collections\n- File: saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n  - In AssignedAttributeReferenceInput, add a new field `collection_slugs: ContainsFilterInput` with description: \"Returns objects with a reference pointing to a collection identified by the given slug.\"\n  - Update validate_attribute_value_reference_input to accept the new key \"collection_slugs\" as a valid reference filter key alongside page_slugs, product_slugs, product_variant_skus, category_slugs, and referenced_ids.\n\n- File: saleor/graphql/schema.graphql\n  - In input AssignedAttributeReferenceInput, add a new field `collectionSlugs: ContainsFilterInput` with the same description as above. Keep naming consistent with existing camelCase for GraphQL schema (collectionSlugs).\n\n2) Shared helpers to fetch attribute values referencing Collections and to normalize global IDs\n- File: saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n  - Add typing import for cast since it will be used in new helper.\n  - Implement collection helpers analogous to existing page/product/category/variant helpers:\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_slugs(slugs: list[str], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids(ids: list[int], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - Private helper _get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_identifiers(field_name: str, identifiers: list[str] | list[int], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n      • Use product_models.Collection filtered by the provided identifiers (slug or id) and return AttributeValue filtered by Exists(collections.filter(id=OuterRef(\"reference_collection_id\"))).\n  - Add clean_up_referenced_global_ids(global_ids: list[str]) -> dict[str, set[int]]\n    - Parse GraphQL global IDs (via graphene.Node.from_global_id) and group the numeric IDs into a dict of sets keyed by GraphQL type names: \"Product\", \"ProductVariant\", \"Page\", \"Category\", and \"Collection\". Return empty sets for missing types.\n  - Extend _has_valid_reference_global_id to treat \"Collection\" as a valid type.\n\n3) Extend page filtering to handle collections\n- File: saleor/graphql/page/filters.py\n  - Import the new helpers: clean_up_referenced_global_ids, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_slugs, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids.\n  - Implement filter_by_contains_referenced_collection_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) following the existing pattern used for categories/pages/products/variants:\n    • If contains_all: return an AND aggregation of per-slug expressions.\n    • If contains_any: return a single expression for all provided slugs.\n  - Extend _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids and _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids to accept an additional parameter collection_ids: set[int], and incorporate expressions built from get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids for both \"all\" (AND) and \"any\" (OR) cases.\n  - Update filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids to:\n    • Replace manual graphene.Node.from_global_id parsing with the new clean_up_referenced_global_ids helper.\n    • Include the new collection_ids set when delegating to the _filter_by_* helpers.\n  - Update filter_objects_by_reference_attributes to handle the new key \"collection_slugs\" by composing with filter_by_contains_referenced_collection_slugs.\n\n4) Extend product filtering to handle collections\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_attributes.py\n  - Import the new helpers: clean_up_referenced_global_ids, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_slugs, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids.\n  - Implement filter_by_contains_referenced_collection_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) similar to the pages and categories filters (both contains_all and contains_any support).\n  - Extend _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids and _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids to accept collection_ids and merge expressions created from get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids accordingly.\n  - Update filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids to use clean_up_referenced_global_ids rather than inline graphene parsing; include collection_ids when calling the _filter_by_* helpers.\n  - Update filter_objects_by_reference_attributes to recognize and process the new \"collection_slugs\" key.\n\n5) Extend product variant filtering to handle collections\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_variant.py\n  - Import the new helpers: clean_up_referenced_global_ids, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_slugs, get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids.\n  - Implement filter_by_contains_referenced_collection_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) mirroring the product and page implementations.\n  - Extend _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids and _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids with collection_ids, composing expressions using get_attribute_values_by_referenced_collection_ids.\n  - Update filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids to use clean_up_referenced_global_ids and include collection_ids.\n  - Update filter_objects_by_reference_attributes to handle \"collection_slugs\".\n\n6) Tests for collection reference filtering\n- Add new tests to validate containsAny/containsAll for both collection slugs and referenced IDs, across pages, products, and variants. Follow existing patterns for similar tests on other entity types:\n  - saleor/graphql/page/tests/queries/pages_with_where/test_with_where_references_collections.py\n  - saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/products_filtrations/test_over_references_collections.py\n  - saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_references_collections.py\n  Each test should:\n    • Create reference-type attributes with entity_type=COLLECTION and assign AttributeValue instances that reference specific collections.\n    • Assign those attribute values to pages/products/variants.\n    • Query using where/filters with `reference.collectionSlugs.containsAny/containsAll` and `reference.referencedIds.containsAny/containsAll` and assert the result counts and identities per the scenarios.\n\nConstraints and consistency:\n- Keep naming conventions consistent: in Python inputs use snake_case keys (collection_slugs) and in SDL use camelCase (collectionSlugs).\n- Reuse existing patterns for pages/products/categories/variants to ensure behavior parity.\n- Ensure all queryset builders use .using(db_connection_name) and Exists/OuterRef patterns consistent with the existing code.\n- Update imports as needed (e.g., remove direct graphene import where replaced by clean_up_referenced_global_ids).",
-      "prompt": "Add support to filter pages, products, and product variants by attribute references to Collections. Users should be able to filter via collection slugs and via referenced global IDs, using both containsAll and containsAny semantics, just like existing filters for pages, products, categories, and variants. Update the GraphQL input to include collectionSlugs in the reference filter, add the missing shared helper functions for fetching attribute values referencing collections, extend filters for pages/products/variants to handle collection slugs and collection IDs, and centralize global ID grouping logic. Include tests covering containsAny and containsAll across pages, products (both where and deprecated filter inputs), and product variants, using reference attributes that point to collections.",
