-      "spec": "Implement image/media validation and handling changes for the ProductBulkCreate mutation.\n\nRequired changes:\n\n1) Update results construction\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/bulk_mutations/product_bulk_create.py\n- Function: get_results\n- Behavior: Build results using a conditional expression per item instead of a list-level conditional so that each result is either:\n  - ProductBulkResult(product=ChannelContext(node=instance, channel_slug=None), errors=errors) when instance is present, or\n  - ProductBulkResult(product=None, errors=errors) when instance is None.\n- Ensure the logic is functionally identical but expressed within each element (no if/else filter on the comprehension itself).\n\n2) Validate media at input-cleaning time and pass GraphQL context\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/bulk_mutations/product_bulk_create.py\n- Method signature change: def clean_media(cls, info, media_inputs, product_index, index_error_map)\n- Caller change: In clean_product_input, when media inputs are present, call cls.clean_media(info, media_inputs, product_index, index_error_map)\n- Behavior for each media item (indexed by i) in media_inputs:\n  - If neither image nor media_url provided: append ProductBulkCreateError with path=f\"media.{i}\", message=\"Image or external URL is required.\", code=ProductBulkCreateErrorCode.REQUIRED.\n  - If both provided: append ProductBulkCreateError with path=f\"media.{i}\", message=\"Either image or external URL is required.\", code=ProductBulkCreateErrorCode.DUPLICATED_INPUT_ITEM.\n  - If alt provided and longer than the limit (ALT_CHAR_LIMIT): append ProductBulkCreateError with path=f\"media.{i}\", code=ProductBulkCreateErrorCode.INVALID, with the existing over-the-limit message.\n  - If image is provided (Upload mapping key):\n    - Replace media_input[\"image\"] with info.context.FILES.get(image)\n    - Run clean_image_file(media_input, \"image\", ProductBulkCreateErrorCode). On ValidationError, call add_indexes_to_errors(product_index, exc, index_error_map, f\"media.{i}\") and skip adding this media item.\n  - Else if media_url is provided and is_image_url(media_url):\n    - Run validate_image_url(media_url, \"media_url\", ProductBulkCreateErrorCode.INVALID.value). On ValidationError, call add_indexes_to_errors(product_index, exc, index_error_map, f\"media.{i}\") and skip this media item.\n    - If valid, compute filename = get_filename_from_url(media_url), fetch bytes with HTTPClient.send_request(\"GET\", media_url, stream=True, timeout=30, allow_redirects=False), wrap as File(response.raw, filename), and set media_input[\"image\"] to that File so downstream code treats it as an uploaded image.\n  - Append the (possibly modified) media_input to media_to_create and return this list.\n\n3) Simplify media persistence to avoid re-validation and network calls\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/bulk_mutations/product_bulk_create.py\n- Method: prepare_media\n- Behavior changes:\n  - For uploaded image (img_data := media_input.get(\"image\")):\n    - Do not read from info.context.FILES or call clean_image_file here. Assume clean_media already validated and transformed the data. Create ProductMedia with image=img_data (plus alt, product, type=IMAGE).\n  - For media_url values:\n    - Only handle non-image URLs (oEmbed). If not is_image_url(media_url), call get_oembed_data and create ProductMedia with external_url and oembed_data accordingly.\n    - Remove the previous branch that validated and fetched image URLs here; images via URL are now converted to files in clean_media.\n\n4) Keep error path formatting stable\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/bulk_mutations/product_bulk_create.py\n- Method: clean_variants\n- Ensure the path field for variant errors uses a single conditional expression wrapped in parentheses: path=(f\"variants.{index}.{error.path}\" if error.path else f\"variants.{index}\"). Functionality remains the same.\n\n5) Extend tests for media validation edge cases and add a test utility\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/tests/mutations/test_product_bulk_create.py\n- Imports: add from unittest.mock import Mock, patch; import PIL; import new helpers from saleor.product.tests.utils.\n- Add tests:\n  - test_product_bulk_create_with_media_invalid_extension: map an uploaded image without a file extension to a product’s media; expect no errors for the valid product, and for the invalid image expect code=INVALID, path=\"media.0.image\", message=\"Lack of file extension.\", count=0.\n  - test_product_bulk_create_with_media_invalid_media_type: map a .jpg filename whose content-type is application/zip; expect code=INVALID, path=\"media.0.image\", message=\"Invalid file type.\", count=0.\n  - test_product_bulk_create_with_media_image_with_invalid_exif: patch saleor.graphql.core.validators.file.Image.open so that getexif raises PIL.UnidentifiedImageError; expect code=INVALID, path=\"media.0.image\", and the message starts with \"Invalid file. The following error was raised during the attempt\"; count=0.\n  - test_product_bulk_create_with_media_with_media_url_invalid_image_type: patch saleor.graphql.core.validators.file.is_supported_image_mimetype to return False and patch HTTPClient to avoid real IO; pass a mediaUrl to an image; expect code=INVALID, path=\"media.0.mediaUrl\", message=\"Invalid file type.\", count=0.\n\n- File: saleor/product/tests/utils.py\n- Add helper function create_image_without_extension(image_name=\"product_img_without_extension\") that returns a SimpleUploadedFile with JPEG content but no file extension in its name.\n- Ensure existing create_zip_file_with_image_ext remains available and unchanged.\n\n6) Wire changes together\n- Ensure clean_product_input passes info to clean_media.\n- Ensure imports remain correct at the top of product_bulk_create.py for HTTPClient, clean_image_file, is_image_url, validate_image_url, get_filename_from_url.\n- Ensure behavior matches tests: errors from image validation map to the nested path under media index (e.g., \"media.0.image\" or \"media.0.mediaUrl\") and maintain exact messages produced by validators.file.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- All updated and new tests in saleor/graphql/product/tests/mutations/test_product_bulk_create.py pass.\n- Uploaded images and image URLs are validated during input cleaning; prepare_media only persists objects.\n- Invalid file extension, invalid mimetype, invalid EXIF, and invalid image type via URL yield ProductBulkCreateError with the expected code, path, and message.\n- get_results returns entries for all inputs regardless of instance presence, using the new conditional expression formulation.\n",
-      "prompt": "We need to improve media handling in the bulk product creation GraphQL mutation. Validate image uploads and image URLs during input cleaning, not during persistence. For each media entry, accept either an uploaded image or a media URL, validate it appropriately, and convert valid image URLs into file objects before saving. Ensure errors are attached to the correct media index and field, and keep alt length limits. Then simplify the media creation step to only create ProductMedia instances without revalidating or refetching. Also adjust the results construction to handle rows with and without instances uniformly. Add tests to cover invalid image extensions, wrong mimetypes (e.g., zip masquerading as jpg), invalid EXIF data, and invalid image types for image URLs, plus a small test helper for generating an image without a file extension. Keep the external (oEmbed) media flow for non-image URLs unchanged.",
