-      "spec": "Implement filtering over attributes referencing Category across pages, products, and variants.\n\nScope and behavior:\n- Support filtering items whose attributes reference Category objects by:\n  - Category slugs via new reference input field categorySlugs\n  - Category global IDs via referencedIds, with Category type accepted\n- Semantics mirror existing page/product/variant reference filters:\n  - containsAll: match only items referencing all specified categories\n  - containsAny: match items referencing at least one specified category\n\nRequired changes:\n1) saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n- In AssignedAttributeReferenceInput, add a new field:\n  - category_slugs: ContainsFilterInput\n    Description: Returns objects with a reference pointing to a category identified by the given slug.\n- Add helpers to fetch AttributeValue rows referencing categories:\n  - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_slugs(slugs: list[str], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n  - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_ids(ids: list[int], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n  - Backed by a private _get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_identifiers(field_name: str, identifiers: list[str|int], db_connection_name: str) using product_models.Category and Exists with OuterRef(\"reference_category_id\").\n- Extend _has_valid_reference_global_id to accept \"Category\" as a valid type for referencedIds.\n- In validate_attribute_value_reference_input(), include \"category_slugs\" alongside existing keys in the allowed reference fields list.\n\n2) saleor/graphql/page/filters.py\n- Import the two new helper functions from shared_filters.\n- Add filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) that:\n  - For contains_all: AND a single-expression filter per slug\n  - For contains_any: OR a single-expression filter over all provided slugs\n  - Use _filter_contains_single_expression with referenced_attr_values resolved via the new helper(s).\n- Update _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids(...) signature and implementation to include category_ids: set[int], AND-ing a single-expression per category ID using get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_ids.\n- Update _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids(...) to include category_ids, OR-ing a single-expression over get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_ids for all IDs.\n- Update filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids(...):\n  - Initialize and populate category_ids when the parsed global ID type is \"Category\".\n  - Pass category_ids to the *_referenced_object_ids helpers for both contains_all and contains_any branches.\n- Update filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(...):\n  - Expand the attr_value type Literal to include \"category_slugs\" and \"collection_slugs\".\n  - When attr_value contains \"category_slugs\", AND-in the result from filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs.\n\n3) saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_attributes.py\n- Import new category helper functions.\n- Add filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) following the same pattern as page filters.\n- Update _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids(...) to include category_ids handling (AND per id using get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_ids).\n- Update _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids(...) to include category_ids handling (OR across get_attribute_values_by_referenced_category_ids).\n- Update filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids(...) to parse Category IDs and pass category_ids to the above helpers.\n- Update filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(...) to include \"category_slugs\" in the allowed Literal, and when present, AND-in the expression from filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs.\n\n4) saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_variant.py\n- Mirror the same changes as in product_attributes.py for variants:\n  - Import helpers, add filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs.\n  - Add category_ids handling to both *_referenced_object_ids helpers.\n  - Parse Category in filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids(...) and pass along category_ids.\n  - Include \"category_slugs\" in the Literal and AND-in filter_by_contains_referenced_category_slugs when present.\n\n5) saleor/graphql/schema.graphql\n- In input AssignedAttributeReferenceInput, add the field:\n  - categorySlugs: ContainsFilterInput\n  - Include the description about referencing categories by slug.\n\nValidation and tests (behavioral):\n- Pages: where attributes reference categories by slug with containsAny returns two matching pages; containsAll returns one; by referencedIds with Category global IDs, containsAny returns three and containsAll returns two (according to sample fixtures).\n- Products: both where and filter queries accept categorySlugs with containsAny/containsAll; referencedIds with Category global IDs behave similarly.\n- Variants: where query accepts categorySlugs and referencedIds with containsAny/containsAll.\n\nNotes:\n- Ensure Category is recognized in global ID validation for referencedIds and properly decoded via graphene.Node.from_global_id.\n- Ensure all new category filter pieces compose via the existing _filter_contains_single_expression helper used for other reference types.\n- Preserve existing behavior for pages/products/variants referencing pages/products/variants.",
-      "prompt": "Add support for filtering pages, products, and product variants by attributes that reference categories. The filters should work with both category slugs and Category global IDs, honoring containsAny and containsAll semantics, and integrate into existing reference attribute filtering for the where/filter inputs. Update the shared GraphQL input and schema to expose a categorySlugs field for reference attributes, ensure Category global IDs are treated as valid in reference filters, and wire category-based conditions into the page, product, and variant filters. Provide tests that cover slug-based and referencedIds-based filtering for containsAny and containsAll.",
