-      "spec": "- Goal: Prevent deadlocks when adding variants to a checkout and ensure consistent GraphQL error behavior if a checkout is removed during mutation execution.\n\nChanges to implement:\n\n1) saleor/checkout/utils.py\n- Update imports:\n  - From ..core.exceptions, also import NonExistingCheckout.\n  - From .lock_objects, also import checkout_qs_select_for_update alongside checkout_lines_qs_select_for_update.\n- In add_variants_to_checkout(checkout, variants, checkout_lines_data, channel, ...):\n  - Wrap the function body in transaction.atomic() as it is now, but first lock the checkout row before touching lines:\n    - Execute checkout_qs_select_for_update().only(\"pk\").get(token=checkout.token) to acquire a SELECT FOR UPDATE lock on the checkout.\n    - If the checkout no longer exists (Checkout.DoesNotExist), raise NonExistingCheckout(checkout.token).\n  - Proceed to lock and fetch checkout lines using checkout_lines_qs_select_for_update(), perform deletes/updates, and bulk_create new lines as currently done.\n  - Keep the bulk_create for to_create without extra locking; it is safe since the checkout row is already locked at the beginning of the transaction.\n\n2) saleor/core/exceptions.py\n- Add a new exception class NonExistingCheckout(Exception):\n  - __init__(self, checkout_token: UUID) stores the token on self.checkout_token and sets the message to: \"Checkout: {checkout_token} doesn't exist.\".\n\n3) saleor/graphql/core/mutations.py\n- Add a module-level constant: MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX = \"Couldn't resolve to a node:\".\n- In BaseMutation.get_node_or_error, when raising the ValidationError for a missing node, change the constructed message to use the new constant so it becomes f\"{MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX} {node_id}\". Ensure all other behavior remains the same.\n\n4) saleor/graphql/checkout/mutations/checkout_lines_add.py\n- Import NonExistingCheckout from ....core.exceptions and MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX from ...core.mutations.\n- In process_lines_input, wrap the add_variants_to_checkout call in try/except NonExistingCheckout.\n  - On catching NonExistingCheckout as e:\n    - Compute graphql_id = graphene.Node.to_global_id(\"Checkout\", e.checkout_token).\n    - Raise a ValidationError with field \"id\" containing a ValidationError message f\"{MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX} {graphql_id}\", and code CheckoutErrorCode.NOT_FOUND.value.\n- Leave the rest of the logic (fetching lines, updating delivery method lists, invalidating) unchanged.\n\n5) saleor/graphql/checkout/mutations/checkout_create.py and checkout_create_from_order.py\n- No behavior change needed related to error handling (the checkout is created within the mutation). Optionally annotate with a comment clarifying why NonExistingCheckout is not handled here.\n\n6) Tests: saleor/graphql/checkout/tests\n- Add tests to verify deleted-checkout race conditions are handled consistently:\n  - In mutations/test_checkout_lines_add.py, add test_checkout_lines_add_checkout_removed_before_adding_variants_to_checkout:\n    - Use saleor.tests.race_condition.RunBefore to patch the add_variants_to_checkout call in the checkout_lines_add mutation and delete the checkout just before it runs.\n    - Assert response has no checkout, the first error’s field is \"id\", code is CheckoutErrorCode.NOT_FOUND, and message equals f\"{MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX} {<checkout global id>}\".\n  - In mutations/test_checkout_lines_update.py, add test_checkout_lines_update_checkout_removed_before_adding_variants_to_checkout with analogous behavior and assertions for the update mutation.\n- Benchmark query counts: update expected counts by +1 where the locking introduces one extra query:\n  - tests/benchmark/test_checkout_mutations.py: increment the django_assert_num_queries values shown in the diff by 1 for the affected tests. Ensure all modified tests expect exactly one more query than before.\n\n7) Ensure existing behavior remains intact\n- NonExistingCheckoutLines handling in CheckoutLinesUpdate stays as-is.\n- Locking helpers in saleor/checkout/lock_objects.py remain unchanged, but the new checkout_qs_select_for_update must be used from utils.add_variants_to_checkout.\n- No changes to GraphQL schemas or return types; only error mapping and query counts are affected.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Adding/updating checkout lines does not deadlock and first locks the checkout row before any line-level locks.\n- If a checkout is removed just before adding/updating lines, mutations return a GraphQL ValidationError on field \"id\" with code NOT_FOUND and a message prefixed by the constant MISSING_NODE_ERROR_MESSAGE_PREFIX, including the checkout’s global ID.\n- New tests for race conditions pass.\n- Updated benchmark query counts pass.\n- Standardized missing node error message is used via the shared constant.",
-      "prompt": "Strengthen checkout line mutations against deadlocks and race conditions. Ensure that when adding or updating lines, the checkout is locked before any line operations, and that if the checkout disappears during processing, the mutations return a NOT_FOUND validation error on the id field with a standardized missing-node message. Introduce a shared constant for the missing-node error prefix and adopt it wherever missing node validation errors are constructed. Add tests simulating checkout deletion just before adding/updating lines to verify consistent error behavior, and adjust checkout-related benchmark tests to account for the additional locking query. Keep all other behavior unchanged.",
