-      "spec": "Implement concurrency-safe checkout price recalculation and update related tests.\n\nScope\n- Core logic: saleor/checkout/calculations.py\n- Fixture: saleor/checkout/tests/fixtures/checkout_with_prices.py\n- Tests: \n  - saleor/checkout/tests/test_calculations.py\n  - saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/benchmark/test_checkout_mutations.py\n  - saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/mutations/test_checkout_lines_update.py\n  - saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/test_checkout.py\n\nRequirements\n1) Concurrency-safe price persistence in _fetch_checkout_prices_if_expired\n- After recomputing prices and setting price_expiration, do not blindly save recalculated totals/lines.\n- Acquire a row lock for the target Checkout using checkout_qs_select_for_update() and filter by token, retrieving only last_change.\n- Behavior when locked checkout not found (deleted or converted to order): skip persistence and return the recalculated checkout_info and lines objects as computed in-memory.\n- When the locked checkout exists, compare the in-memory checkout.last_change to locked_checkout.last_change. Only if they are equal (no concurrent update occurred) persist:\n  - Save Checkout with the specific update_fields used for totals, shipping, discount fields, currency, last_change, price_expiration, and tax_error.\n  - Bulk update CheckoutLine fields (total_price_net_amount, total_price_gross_amount, tax_rate, undiscounted_unit_price_amount, prior_unit_price_amount) via checkout_lines_bulk_update.\n- If last_change differs, skip saving and return the recalculated objects.\n- Perform the above inside allow_writer() and transaction.atomic().\n- Update imports in calculations.py to reference:\n  - from . import CheckoutAuthorizeStatus, base_calculations\n  - from .lock_objects import checkout_qs_select_for_update\n\n2) Stabilize checkout_with_prices fixture\n- In saleor/checkout/tests/fixtures/checkout_with_prices.py, when setting shipping method on checkout_with_items, also set checkout country from address_other_country and save both shipping_method and country fields in a single save (commit=False on set_country).\n\n3) Add race-condition tests for recalculation\n- In saleor/checkout/tests/test_calculations.py, add tests that:\n  a) Delete checkout between tax calculation and save, using race_condition.RunAfter on saleor.checkout.calculations._calculate_and_add_tax to delete the row. Verify:\n     - refresh_from_db raises DoesNotExist\n     - the returned checkout_info/lines contain recalculated non-zero prices different from initial values.\n  b) Modify checkout (increase line quantities using F and change email) between tax calculation and save. Verify:\n     - returned checkout_info/lines reflect recalculated prices based on the original snapshot values\n     - DB has the concurrent modifications (email updated, quantities incremented)\n     - recalculated values were not persisted over those changes.\n- Ensure tests import F, Checkout, and race_condition helpers, and use get_plugins_manager, fetch_checkout_lines/info, zero_taxed_money.\n\n4) GraphQL tests for behavior under concurrent update\n- In saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/test_checkout.py:\n  - Extend checkout pricing query selection to include lines.quantity.\n  - Add a test that patches saleor.checkout.calculations._calculate_and_add_tax and fetch_checkout_data (wraps) and simulates a concurrent modification (update email and increment quantities) during recalculation via race_condition.RunAfter.\n  - Assert fetch_checkout_data is called more than once (retries/flow) but _calculate_and_add_tax is executed exactly once, final DB reflects concurrent change, and response data shows recalculated totals and pre-update line quantities.\n- In saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/mutations/test_checkout_lines_update.py:\n  - Add analogous test around checkoutLinesUpdate mutation: simulate concurrent email update during recalculation and assert multiple fetch calls, single tax calc call, no errors, and DB email updated.\n\n5) Update benchmark query counts\n- Increase the expected django_assert_num_queries counts by +1 in the affected GraphQL benchmark tests under saleor/graphql/checkout/tests/benchmark/test_checkout_mutations.py for create/update/add lines mutations where the additional select_for_update query occurs.\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- Recalculation returns fresh prices in response objects even if the checkout was concurrently modified or deleted, but does not overwrite concurrent DB changes.\n- When no concurrent modifications occur, recalculated prices are persisted to Checkout and CheckoutLine with the specified update fields.\n- The new and updated tests pass, including the increased benchmark query counts.\n- All database writes are wrapped in allow_writer() and a single transaction.atomic() block for the save path.\n",
-      "prompt": "Make checkout price recalculation resilient to concurrent updates. When prices are expired and a request recomputes totals, ensure that saving those recalculated values does not overwrite changes made by other requests or fail if the checkout was removed. Lock the checkout row, detect if it changed during the recalculation window, and skip persisting if it was updated or deleted, while still returning recalculated data in the response. Update tests to simulate these races, verify that recalculated values are returned without clobbering concurrent DB updates, and adjust expected query counts impacted by the additional lock. Also ensure the checkout-with-prices fixture sets a country consistently with its address so shipping/tax behavior is stable.",
