-      "spec": "Implement a new GraphQL interface for objects with attributes and apply it to Product, ProductVariant, and Page. Update the schema and tests accordingly.\n\nRequired changes:\n1) Define the ObjectWithAttributes interface\n- File: saleor/graphql/attribute/types.py\n- Add a new class ObjectWithAttributes(BaseInterface) with:\n  - Field assigned_attribute: graphene.Field(AssignedAttribute)\n    - Argument: slug: graphene.String (required, with description \"Slug of the attribute\")\n    - Description: \"Get a single attribute attached to the object by attribute slug.\" + ADDED_IN_322\n  - Field assigned_attributes: NonNullList(AssignedAttribute)\n    - Required: True\n    - Description: \"List of attributes assigned to the object.\" + ADDED_IN_322\n    - Argument: limit: PositiveInt with description \"Maximum number of attributes to return. Default is {DEFAULT_NESTED_LIST_LIMIT}.\" and default_value=DEFAULT_NESTED_LIST_LIMIT\n  - Meta: description = \"An object with attributes.\" + ADDED_IN_322, doc_category = DOC_CATEGORY_ATTRIBUTES\n- Do not add resolvers in the interface; concrete types already expose resolve_assigned_attribute(s).\n\n2) Apply ObjectWithAttributes to Page\n- File: saleor/graphql/page/types.py\n- Update imports to include ObjectWithAttributes from ..attribute.types\n- In Page.Meta.interfaces, append ObjectWithAttributes to the existing [graphene.relay.Node, ObjectWithMetadata]\n- No field or resolver changes are required here since Page already defines assigned_attribute(s) and has resolvers.\n\n3) Apply ObjectWithAttributes to Product and ProductVariant; simplify ProductVariant.assignedAttributes arguments\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/types/products.py\n- Update imports to include ObjectWithAttributes from ...attribute.types\n- In Product.Meta.interfaces, append ObjectWithAttributes to the existing [relay.Node, ObjectWithMetadata]\n- In ProductVariant.Meta.interfaces, append ObjectWithAttributes to the existing [relay.Node, ObjectWithMetadata]\n- In ProductVariant.assigned_attributes field definition, remove the variant_selection argument entirely; retain the limit: PositiveInt argument with the existing description and default\n- In ProductVariant.resolve_assigned_attributes, remove the variant_selection parameter from the resolver signature. Inside the resolver set variant_selection = None and call _resolve_attributes(root, info, variant_selection, limit)\n- Do not change ProductVariant.attributes field (it still supports variantSelection) and do not change existing resolvers for assigned_attribute(s) on Product and ProductVariant beyond the above signature tweak.\n\n4) Update schema.graphql to reflect the interface and argument changes\n- File: saleor/graphql/schema.graphql\n- Add a new interface ObjectWithAttributes @doc(category: \"Attributes\") with:\n  - assignedAttribute(slug: String!): AssignedAttribute and description matching types\n  - assignedAttributes(limit: PositiveInt = 100): [AssignedAttribute!]! and matching description\n- Update type Product, ProductVariant, and Page to implement ObjectWithAttributes (\"implements Node & ObjectWithMetadata & ObjectWithAttributes\")\n- Ensure the ProductVariant.assignedAttributes field no longer accepts variantSelection; confirm the signature only includes limit: PositiveInt = 100\n- Ensure the AssignedAttribute interface remains defined under the Attributes category and that PositiveInt scalar is present\n- Remove duplicated assignedAttribute/assignedAttributes field definitions directly on Product, ProductVariant, Page in sections where they became redundant due to implementing the interface (keep the resolvers in type classes).\n\n5) Update tests to align with the new interface and removed argument\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/test_variant_query.py\n  - In query definitions, remove variantSelection from assignedAttributes usages\n  - Remove assertions that check assignedAttributes length filtering by variantSelection; keep and focus on attributes field for variantSelection filtering where applicable\n- File: saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/test_product_variant_query.py\n  - Remove the test that used assignedAttributes(limit: 1, variantSelection: ...) to validate limit with filtering (test_applies_limit_on_product_assigned_attributes)\n  - Clean up unused imports (pytest, VariantAttributeScope) related to the removed test\n\nBehavioral expectations after changes:\n- Product, ProductVariant, and Page all expose assignedAttribute(slug: String!) and assignedAttributes(limit: PositiveInt = 100) by virtue of ObjectWithAttributes, consistent descriptions and doc categories\n- ProductVariant.assignedAttributes no longer supports variantSelection filter; any variant selection filtering remains on the attributes field only\n- Existing assignedAttribute(s) resolvers on Product, ProductVariant, and Page continue to function; the interface adds shared schema, not new logic\n- The schema.graphql matches these structures and no duplicate field definitions remain on concrete types in the schema output where the interface now defines them\n- Tests compile and pass with updated queries and assertions",
