-      "spec": "Implement a refactor that relocates page-attribute filtering logic from the shared attribute module into the page module and updates imports accordingly.\n\nMake the following changes:\n\n1) In saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n- Remove high-level filtering functions that build Q expressions for both pages and products. Specifically delete:\n  - filter_objects_by_attributes\n  - filter_objects_by_reference_attributes\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids\n  - _filter_contains_single_expression\n  - _filter_contains_all_condition\n  - _filter_contains_any_condition\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_pages\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_products\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_variants\n  - filter_by_slug_or_name\n  - filter_by_numeric_attribute\n  - filter_by_boolean_attribute\n  - filter_by_date_attribute\n  - filter_by_date_time_attribute\n- Retain and continue exporting only:\n  - GraphQL input classes for attribute where input\n  - Validation functions (validate_attribute_value_input, validate_attribute_value_reference_input)\n  - AttributeValue getter utilities (get_attribute_values_by_*), including for slug/name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time, and referenced pages/products/variants (by ids/slugs/skus)\n- Update imports to remove unused Q (keep Exists, OuterRef, QuerySet).\n\n2) In saleor/graphql/page/filters.py\n- Replace the previous delegation to shared filter_objects_by_attributes with a page-specific implementation and add the necessary helpers:\n  - Add _get_assigned_page_attribute_for_attribute_value(attribute_values, db_connection_name) that returns a Q(Exists(...)) over AssignedPageAttributeValue with a value_id subquery.\n  - Implement page-local filter helpers that return Q expressions by leveraging the shared AttributeValue getter utilities:\n    - filter_by_slug_or_name(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_numeric_attribute(attr_id, numeric_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_boolean_attribute(attr_id, boolean_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_date_attribute(attr_id, date_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_date_time_attribute(attr_id, date_value, db_connection_name)\n  - Implement reference attribute helpers for pages:\n    - _filter_contains_single_expression(attr_id, db_connection_name, referenced_attr_values) that optionally filters by attribute_id and wraps with _get_assigned_page_attribute_for_attribute_value\n    - filter_by_contains_referenced_page_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_contains_referenced_product_slugs(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name)\n    - filter_by_contains_referenced_variant_skus(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name)\n    - _filter_by_contains_all_referenced_object_ids(...) and _filter_by_contains_any_referenced_object_ids(...) that combine page/product/variant references using AND/OR semantics\n    - filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) that parses GraphQL global IDs (Page/Product/ProductVariant) via graphene.Node.from_global_id and delegates to the helper above\n    - filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name) that composes referenced_ids, page_slugs, product_slugs, and product_variant_skus filters\n  - Re-implement filter_pages_by_attributes(qs, value) locally for pages, mirroring the prior generic flow:\n    - Resolve attribute slugs to Attribute rows, short-circuit to qs.none() for any unknown slug\n    - If a filter has a slug without a value, produce a Q expression matching any assigned value for that attribute via AssignedPageAttributeValue\n    - For filters with value, branch by the provided value key (slug, name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time, reference) and compose Q expressions using the page-local helpers\n    - If any composed expression exists, return qs.filter(expression), else qs.none()\n- Update imports in this file to include:\n  - typing.Literal\n  - django.db.models: Exists, OuterRef, Q, QuerySet\n  - Attribute and AttributeValue models\n  - From ..attribute.shared_filters: AssignedAttributeWhereInput, CONTAINS_TYPING, all get_attribute_values_by_* helpers, and validate_attribute_value_input\n  - From ..utils.filters: Number and existing filter helpers\n- Keep PageWhere.is_valid calling validate_attribute_value_input unchanged.\n\n3) Ensure no remaining references to the deleted shared functions exist in page filters. Product filters keep their own local versions and do not import the removed shared functions, so no changes are required outside the two edited files.\n\n4) Behavior and API expectations\n- GraphQL where filtering for pages by attributes must continue to support:\n  - slug/name string filters, numeric/boolean/date/date_time filters, and reference filters with contains_all/contains_any for referenced_ids (global IDs) or page_slugs/product_slugs/product_variant_skus\n  - Mixed attribute inputs across multiple attributes combining with logical AND\n  - Attributes provided without a value returning pages that have any value for that attribute\n- Validation of attribute value input remains in shared_filters and is invoked in PageWhere.is_valid.\n\n5) Lint/typing hygiene\n- Because shared_filters.py no longer constructs Q expressions, remove the unused Q import and any other unused imports in that file.\n- In page/filters.py add the new imports and ensure type hints: QuerySet[AttributeValue] where applicable, and Number for numeric filters.",
-      "prompt": "Refactor page attribute filtering so that page-specific logic lives in the page module, not the shared attribute module. The shared module should expose only reusable input types, validations, and AttributeValue queryset helpers. Implement all page-side filtering helpers in the page filters file, using the shared getter utilities to build Exists/OuterRef expressions against AssignedPageAttributeValue. Support slug/name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time, and reference filters (including containsAll/containsAny with global IDs and with page/product/variant identifiers). Ensure PageWhere continues to validate attribute inputs, and that filtering behavior is unchanged from a client perspective. Remove now-unused imports from the shared file and add the necessary imports to the page file.",
