-      "spec": "Implement reference-based attribute filtering for ProductVariant.where.attributes.reference.\n\nScope\n- Add reference filtering helpers for AttributeValue lookups by referenced Page/Product/Variant identifiers.\n- Extend variant attribute filtering to support reference filters (by page slugs, product slugs, variant skus, and global IDs for Page/Product/ProductVariant).\n- Update validation to accept only correct reference inputs and reject empty/invalid combinations.\n- Add tests that verify filtering semantics and validation errors.\n\nFiles to change\n1) saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n- Add helper functions to resolve AttributeValue by reference targets:\n  - Internal generic helpers for pages/products/variants by identifier, then public wrappers:\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_page_slugs(slugs, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_page_ids(ids, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_product_slugs(slugs, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_product_ids(ids, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_variant_skus(slugs, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    - get_attribute_values_by_referenced_variant_ids(ids, db_connection_name) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n  - Each should query the referenced model (Page/Product/ProductVariant) using the given identifiers against the relevant field (slug/id/sku), and return AttributeValue filtered by Exists(...) where the AttributeValue.reference_*_id matches OuterRef on the referenced queryset.\n- Ensure the CONTAINS_TYPING alias is available for import in product_variant filters: dict[Literal[\"contains_any\",\"contains_all\"], list[str]].\n- Ensure validate_attribute_value_input already validates the 'reference' value input:\n  - For attributes with input_type != REFERENCE, using 'reference' must be rejected.\n  - For 'reference', accept only one of 'referencedIds', 'pageSlugs', 'productSlugs', 'productVariantSkus'. Inside each, accept only one of containsAll or containsAny, and arrays must be non-null and non-empty.\n  - Raise GraphQLError messages aligned with tests when: value is empty/null, multiple keys provided, mismatched input types, both containsAll and containsAny provided, or contains* provided with empty list.\n\n2) saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_variant.py\n- Import typing.Literal.\n- Import CONTAINS_TYPING and the new shared_filters getters for referenced pages/products/variants.\n- Implement reference filter builders that return Q expressions:\n  - _filter_contains_single_expression(attr_id, db_connection_name, referenced_attr_values):\n    - Optionally restrict referenced_attr_values to the given attr_id.\n    - Build Exists subquery checking AssignedVariantAttributeValue where value__in referenced_attr_values and assignment_id=OuterRef(\"id\"); then wrap with Exists over AssignedVariantAttribute for the variant (variant_id=OuterRef(\"pk\")).\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_page_slugs(attr_id, attr_value: CONTAINS_TYPING, db_connection_name):\n    - For containsAll: AND multiple single expressions each built with a single slug;\n      For containsAny: one expression over all slugs.\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_product_slugs(...): same pattern for products.\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_variant_skus(...): same pattern for variants.\n  - filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids(attr_id, attr_value: CONTAINS_TYPING, db_connection_name):\n    - Decode global IDs using graphene.Node.from_global_id, bucket into page_ids, product_ids, variant_ids sets.\n    - For containsAll: build AND expression requiring presence of each referenced object by ID using get_attribute_values_by_referenced_*_ids.\n    - For containsAny: build OR expression across the groups using batched ID queries.\n  - filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name): compose Q by intersecting (AND) results of any present keys among referencedIds, pageSlugs, productSlugs, productVariantSkus.\n- Integrate into filter_variants_by_attributes:\n  - When a given attribute filter has value.reference, apply attr_filter_expression &= filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(attr_id, attr_value[\"reference\"], qs.db).\n  - Keep existing behavior for slug/name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time unchanged.\n\n3) Tests\n- Modify saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_multiple_arguments.py\n  - Add parameterized test test_product_variants_query_with_multiple_attribute_referenced_ids verifying containsAny yields 3 results and containsAll yields 1, using a mix of referenced Product, Page, and ProductVariant global IDs. Ensure combinations work across multiple attributes.\n- Add new files and tests:\n  - saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_references_pages.py\n    - Tests for page reference by slug within a specific attribute slug and across attributes; validate containsAny and containsAll semantics and counts.\n    - Tests for filtering by referencedIds (global IDs) within a page-reference attribute slug.\n  - saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_references_products.py\n    - Similar tests for product references by product slugs and by referencedIds.\n  - saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_references_variants.py\n    - Similar tests for variant references by productVariantSkus and by referencedIds.\n- Update saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/test_over_validation.py\n  - Extend invalid input cases to include various malformed 'reference' inputs:\n    - Empty reference structures, None values, empty containsAll/containsAny arrays, providing both containsAll and containsAny, and using 'reference' with non-reference attributes. Ensure tests assert GraphQL errors and null data for productVariants as in the diff.\n\nBehavioral requirements\n- Filtering by attributes.value.reference applies regardless of whether the attribute slug is provided:\n  - If slug is provided, restrict matching to that attribute; if not, match any attribute of input_type REFERENCE assigned to the variant.\n- containsAll means the variant must have at least one assigned attribute value referencing each specified target (all of them), possibly across values and attributes; containsAny means the variant must have at least one assigned attribute value referencing any of the targets listed.\n- For referencedIds, decode global IDs and support Page, Product, ProductVariant; ignore unsupported types.\n- Performance: use Exists subqueries scoped to qs.db; do not fetch full rows; use .using(db_connection_name) for all queries.\n\nNon-goals\n- Do not change legacy ProductVariantFilterInput logic.\n- Do not change other object filters (products/pages).",
-      "prompt": "Add support for filtering product variants by reference-type attribute values in the productVariants(where: ...) API. Extend the attributes value input to accept a reference filter that can specify page slugs, product slugs, variant SKUs, or global IDs of Pages/Products/ProductVariants, each with containsAll or containsAny semantics. Build efficient Exists-based query expressions that match variants having assigned attribute values that reference the requested targets, respecting the attribute slug when provided and working across attributes when not. Validate the reference input so it rejects empty or malformed values and conflicting operators. Provide tests that cover reference filtering over pages, products, and variants, for both containsAny and containsAll, and tests that assert validation errors for invalid inputs.",
