-      "spec": "Implement optional attribute slug in page where filtering and support value-only filters:\n\n1) GraphQL schema input\n- In saleor/graphql/schema.graphql, change AttributePageWhereInput.slug from required to optional (slug: String). Keep the existing description.\n- Reflect the same in the Graphene class: in saleor/graphql/page/filters.py, class AttributePageWhereInput, set slug to required=False.\n\n2) Filtering behavior when slug is omitted\n- In saleor/graphql/page/filters.py, generalize all attribute-specific filter helpers to accept an optional attribute ID:\n  - Update signatures to accept attr_id: int | None for: filter_by_slug_or_name, filter_by_numeric_attribute, filter_by_boolean_attribute, filter_by_date_attribute, filter_by_date_time_attribute.\n  - When attr_id is provided, restrict AttributeValue queryset by attribute_id=attr_id. When attr_id is None, do not filter by attribute_id.\n  - For type-specific filters (numeric/boolean/date/date_time), ensure the AttributeValue queryset additionally restricts by attribute__input_type matching the respective type.\n  - Construct AssignedPageAttributeValue filtering using value__in=<prepared AttributeValue queryset> together with page_id=OuterRef(\"id\"); wrap with Q(Exists(...)).\n\n3) filter_pages_by_attributes to support value-only inputs\n- In saleor/graphql/page/filters.py, adjust filter_pages_by_attributes(qs, value) to:\n  - Build the attribute_slugs set only from inputs that include a slug key and fetch attributes_map from the DB for those slugs.\n  - Handle inputs that provide a slug without a value as the “has any value assigned” case separately.\n  - For each remaining input (including those without slug), branch based on which key is present inside \"value\": slug, name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time, or reference.\n  - For each item, compute attr_id from attributes_map if slug present; otherwise attr_id=None. Pass attr_id to the respective helper (slug/name, numeric, boolean, date, date_time, reference) and combine all results with logical AND.\n  - If no expression is built, return the original queryset; otherwise apply the combined filter.\n\n4) Validation changes for attribute where inputs\n- In saleor/graphql/page/filters.py, update validate_attribute_value_input to support optional slug and index-based error reporting:\n  - Build slug_list only from entries that include a slug; still detect duplicate slugs and raise the existing duplicated-slug error.\n  - Iterate inputs with their index; treat these as invalid and collect their positions: missing both slug and value; slug provided as null; value provided but empty or null.\n  - For entries with a value, enforce that only one key is present inside value; otherwise collect the index for the \"only one input key\" error.\n  - For type-specific validation, only validate the value key against attribute.input_type when a slug is present (build a mapping of slug -> (index, value_key) and fetch attributes by slug). If mismatched, collect the index for the type-mismatch error.\n  - For reference values, collect (index, reference_dict) and pass to the reference validator.\n  - Raise GraphQLError with updated messages that reference \"positions\" (indexes) instead of slugs for: empty/null value, multiple keys, and type mismatches, using the phrasing shown in the diff.\n\n- Update validate_attribute_value_reference_input to accept a list of (index_str, reference_dict | None) and enforce:\n  - If value is falsy/None, collect index in an \"invalid input type\" error that indicates a missing containsAll/containsAny key.\n  - Disallow providing both containsAll and containsAny for the same reference target; collect index for a duplication error.\n  - Disallow empty lists for containsAll/containsAny; collect index for an empty-value error.\n  - Raise GraphQLError with messages referencing positions and following the updated phrasing.\n\n5) Integration with where filterset\n- Ensure PageWhere continues to:\n  - Expose attributes as a ListObjectTypeWhereFilter(input_class=AttributePageWhereInput) that calls filter_pages_by_attributes.\n  - Invoke validate_attribute_value_input in is_valid when attributes are present.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- The pages query supports where: { attributes: [{ value: { slug/name/numeric/boolean/date/dateTime/reference: ... } }] } without providing a slug and returns correct results by applying the value filter across attributes of matching input types.\n- All basic value fields (name, slug) work with and without attribute slug; numeric/date/datetime/boolean value filters operate correctly including range and oneOf; reference filters support referencedIds, pageSlugs, productSlugs, productVariantSkus with containsAny/containsAll semantics.\n- Validation errors reference input positions (indexes) and not slugs; messages match the updated phrasing for empty/null values, multiple value keys, type mismatches, and invalid reference inputs.\n- Existing behavior with an explicit slug remains supported with no regressions.",
-      "prompt": "Make attribute slug optional in the pages where filtering API so that clients can filter pages by attribute values even when they don't know the attribute slug. When a slug is provided, filter within that attribute only; when omitted, apply the value filter across all attributes of the appropriate input type. Update validation to operate on list positions, reporting clear errors for empty inputs, multiple value keys, type mismatches, and malformed reference filters. Ensure the schema reflects the optional slug, helper filters and validators are updated accordingly, and that reference, numeric, boolean, date, dateTime, and basic name/slug filters all work with or without the attribute slug.",
