-      "spec": "Implement productVariants filtering by associated attributes via GraphQL where filters.\n\nMake the following changes:\n\n1) saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py\n- Import Number from ..utils/filters.\n- Add helper functions that return QuerySet[AttributeValue] for reuse in variant filters without embedding assignment logic:\n  - get_attribute_values_by_slug_or_name_value(attr_id: int|None, attr_value: dict, db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    • If attr_id provided, scope to that attribute.\n    • If attr_value contains slug and/or name, apply filter_where_by_value_field on those fields.\n  - get_attribute_values_by_numeric_value(attr_id: int|None, numeric_value: dict[str, Number|list[Number]|dict[str, Number]], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    • Scope to AttributeInputType.NUMERIC and attr_id when provided.\n    • Apply filter_where_by_numeric_field on the numeric field.\n  - get_attribute_values_by_boolean_value(attr_id: int|None, boolean_value: bool, db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    • Scope to AttributeInputType.BOOLEAN (and attr_id if provided) and filter boolean field equal to the provided value.\n  - get_attribute_values_by_date_value(attr_id: int|None, date_value: dict[str, str], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    • Scope to AttributeInputType.DATE\n    • Apply filter_range_field on \"date_time__date\".\n  - get_attribute_values_by_date_time_value(attr_id: int|None, date_value: dict[str, str], db_connection_name: str) -> QuerySet[AttributeValue]\n    • Scope to AttributeInputType.DATE_TIME\n    • Apply filter_range_field on \"date_time\".\n- Do not alter existing page/product assignment-specific filter helpers or validate_attribute_value_input; the new functions are additive and will be consumed by the variant filtering logic.\n\n2) saleor/graphql/product/filters/product_variant.py\n- Update imports:\n  • Import QuerySet from django.db.models.query.\n  • Import AssignedVariantAttribute, AssignedVariantAttributeValue, Attribute, AttributeValue from ....attribute.models.\n  • Import AssignedAttributeWhereInput, validate_attribute_value_input and the new helper functions from ...attribute/shared_filters.\n  • Import ListObjectTypeWhereFilter from ...core/filters.\n  • Import Number from ...utils/filters.\n- Implement helper function to turn AttributeValue queryset into a variant-level Q expression:\n  • _get_assigned_variant_attribute_for_attribute_value_qs(attribute_values: QuerySet[AttributeValue], db_connection_name: str) -> Q\n    – Build a subquery on AssignedVariantAttributeValue filtered by value__in attribute_values and assignment_id=OuterRef(\"id\").\n    – Exists over AssignedVariantAttribute with Exists(assigned_attr_value) and variant_id=OuterRef(\"pk\").\n- Implement filter helpers that use the new shared_filters getters and return Q via the above helper:\n  • filter_by_slug_or_name(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name)\n  • filter_by_numeric_attribute(attr_id, numeric_value, db_connection_name)\n  • filter_by_boolean_attribute(attr_id, boolean_value, db_connection_name)\n  • filter_by_date_attribute(attr_id, date_value, db_connection_name)\n  • filter_by_date_time_attribute(attr_id, date_value, db_connection_name)\n- Implement filter_variants_by_attributes(qs: QuerySet[ProductVariant], value: list[dict]) -> QuerySet[ProductVariant]\n  • Resolve provided attribute slugs to Attribute records using qs.db; if any provided slug is not found, return qs.none().\n  • Support two cases per input element: with slug and value, and with slug only (meaning: any value of that attribute).\n  • For slug-only entries, gather all AttributeValue for those attributes and include variants having any of those values (via the assignment Q expression).\n  • For entries with value: route to the appropriate filter based on key present in value (slug/name -> slug/name; numeric -> numeric; boolean -> boolean; date -> date; date_time -> dateTime). Combine conditions with AND across inputs.\n  • Return qs.filter(combined_expression); if there is no condition, return qs (or qs.none() per original diff – follow the diff logic which returns qs.filter(expr)).\n- Extend ProductVariantWhere:\n  • Add attributes = ListObjectTypeWhereFilter(input_class=AssignedAttributeWhereInput, method=\"filter_attributes\", help_text=\"Filter by attributes associated with the variant.\" + ADDED_IN_322)\n  • Add filter_attributes(qs, _, value) to call filter_variants_by_attributes when value provided.\n  • Override is_valid to call validate_attribute_value_input(self.data[\"attributes\"], self.queryset.db) when attributes present, then super().is_valid().\n\n3) saleor/graphql/schema.graphql\n- In input ProductVariantWhereInput, add:\n  \"\"\"\n  Filter by attributes associated with the variant.\n  \n  Added in Saleor 3.22.\n  \"\"\"\n  attributes: [AssignedAttributeWhereInput!]\n- Ensure AssignedAttributeWhereInput input type is defined once (move it above or reuse the existing definition) with fields:\n  • slug: String\n  • value: AssignedAttributeValueInput — description must state that only one value input field is allowed; providing more than one raises an error.\n- Remove any duplicated AssignedAttributeWhereInput definition blocks from elsewhere in the schema file to avoid duplicates.\n\n4) Tests – add new test suite for variants where attributes:\n- Create directory saleor/graphql/product/tests/queries/variants_where/ with:\n  • __init__.py (empty)\n  • shared.py defining PRODUCT_VARIANTS_WHERE_QUERY: a query with variables where: ProductVariantWhereInput and channel.\n  • test_over_attributes.py – tests variant query over attribute slug, value slug/name, with/without attribute slug provided, asserting counts and specific IDs.\n  • test_over_attributes_boolean.py – tests boolean attributes across two attributes with slug and without, checking counts and specific id match.\n  • test_over_attributes_date.py – tests date attribute filters using date range, name/slug matching, with and without explicit attribute slug; assert counts.\n  • test_over_attributes_datetime.py – similar for dateTime field; include both with slug and without, test ranges and slug/name matching; assert counts.\n  • test_over_attributes_numeric.py – tests numeric eq, oneOf, range, as well as name/slug string matching for numeric values; with and without explicit attribute slug; assert counts.\n  • test_over_multiple_arguments.py – tests negative cases (non-matching attribute/value, multiple attributes with one non-existing) expecting 0 results and combination of multiple attributes expecting specific counts.\n  • test_over_validation.py – tests various invalid inputs for type-specific mismatches, empty/null value, duplicated attr slug, multiple keys in value, and ensures GraphQL errors are returned and data.productVariants is None.\n- Tests should use associate_attribute_values_to_instance from saleor.attribute.utils, get_graphql_content helper, and existing fixtures (e.g., staff_api_client, product_variant_list, weight_attribute, channel_USD, etc.). Names and shapes as in the diff to ensure compatibility with existing test fixtures.\n\n5) CHANGELOG.md\n- Under the relevant features section, add a bullet:\n  - Add support for filtering `productVariants` by associated attributes\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- GraphQL schema exposes ProductVariantWhereInput.attributes with help text and is included in introspection.\n- Filtering productVariants works for slug/name/numeric/boolean/date/dateTime value filters and for slug-only (any value) conditions, combining inputs with AND semantics.\n- Invalid inputs (null/empty values, multiple value keys, mismatched input type for attribute by slug, duplicated slugs) are rejected with GraphQL errors as validated by validate_attribute_value_input.\n- All newly added tests pass, and no duplicates of AssignedAttributeWhereInput exist in the schema.\n- The CHAN