-      "spec": "Refactor and centralize attribute filtering and validation logic into the shared attribute GraphQL module, and update page filters to delegate to it.\n\nMake these changes:\n\n1) saleor/graphql/attribute/shared_filters.py (add shared filtering and validation)\n- Add imports: GraphQLError from graphql; AttributeInputType from saleor.attribute; and from ..utils.filters import filter_range_field, filter_where_by_numeric_field, filter_where_by_value_field.\n- Implement model-agnostic filter builders that return filter expressions for use with QuerySet.filter, each accepting: attr_id (int|None), the value payload, db_connection_name, assigned_attr_model (e.g., AssignedPageAttributeValue), and assigned_id_field_name (e.g., \"page_id\"):\n  • filter_by_slug_or_name(...): Build an AttributeValue queryset filtered by slug/name and optional attribute_id; build an Exists subquery over assigned_attr_model constrained by the assigned_id_field_name; return a filter expression to AND with Q objects.\n  • filter_by_numeric_attribute(...): Limit AttributeValue to input_type NUMERIC and filter via filter_where_by_numeric_field on the \"numeric\" field; wrap with an Exists over assigned_attr_model; return a Q-compatible expression.\n  • filter_by_boolean_attribute(...): Limit AttributeValue to input_type BOOLEAN and boolean value; wrap with Exists over assigned_attr_model; return a Q-compatible expression.\n  • filter_by_date_attribute(...): Limit AttributeValue to input_type DATE and filter via filter_range_field on field \"date_time__date\"; wrap with Exists over assigned_attr_model; return a Q-compatible expression.\n  • filter_by_date_time_attribute(...): Limit AttributeValue to input_type DATE_TIME and filter via filter_range_field on field \"date_time\"; wrap with Exists over assigned_attr_model and return a filter expression suitable for composition with other filters.\n- Implement filtering for reference attributes by composing shared reference helpers already present in this module:\n  • filter_objects_by_reference_attributes(attr_id, attr_value, db_connection_name, assigned_attr_model, assigned_id_field_name): Combine results of filter_by_contains_referenced_object_ids, filter_by_contains_referenced_pages, filter_by_contains_referenced_products, and filter_by_contains_referenced_variants based on keys present in attr_value (\"referenced_ids\", \"page_slugs\", \"product_slugs\", \"product_variant_skus\"). Return a combined Q expression.\n- Implement a generic attribute filter orchestrator:\n  • filter_objects_by_attributes(qs, value, assigned_attr_model, assigned_id_field_name):\n    - Resolve provided attribute slugs to Attribute instances using qs.db. If any provided slug doesn’t exist, return qs.none().\n    - If an entry contains only a slug (no value), include a condition that the entity has any value for that attribute (Exists over assigned attribute values).\n    - For value-provided entries, detect which single key is present and combine corresponding filter expressions: slug/name (via filter_by_slug_or_name), numeric, boolean, date, date_time, or reference (via filter_objects_by_reference_attributes). Always use the db alias from qs.db and the provided assigned model/id field.\n    - If any expressions were built, return qs.filter(combined_expression); otherwise return qs.none().\n- Move and expose validation helpers (ensuring identical behavior/messages as previously in page filters):\n  • validate_attribute_value_reference_input(index_with_values): Validate that each reference filter supplies exactly one of containsAll/containsAny, and that the lists are non-empty; raise GraphQLError using the same error messages, listing offending positions as comma-separated indices.\n  • validate_attribute_value_input(attributes, db_connection_name): Validate the attribute where input list by enforcing: no duplicate slugs; slug cannot be null; value cannot be empty or null; value must contain only one key; when a type-specific value key (numeric, date, date_time, boolean, reference) is used alongside a slug, check the attribute’s input_type from the DB by slug; collect reference values and pass to validate_attribute_value_reference_input; raise GraphQLError with the same messages for each violation.\n- Keep/define CONTAINS_TYPING = dict[Literal[\"contains_any\", \"contains_all\"], list[str]] in this file for reference filters.\n\n2) saleor/graphql/page/filters.py (delegate to shared filters)\n- Remove locally defined attribute filter/validation functions and related imports (e.g., Literal, Exists, OuterRef, GraphQLError, AttributeInputType, Attribute, AttributeValue; and utilities no longer needed like filter_range_field and filter_where_by_numeric_field).\n- Import from ..attribute.shared_filters: AssignedAttributeWhereInput, filter_objects_by_attributes, validate_attribute_value_input. Keep AssignedPageAttributeValue import.\n- Replace filter_pages_by_attributes(qs, value) to return filter_objects_by_attributes(qs, value, AssignedPageAttributeValue, \"page_id\").\n- In PageWhere (where filter class), keep metadata-related behavior, ensure filter_attributes returns filter_pages_by_attributes, and is_valid validates attributes via validate_attribute_value_input(attributes, self.queryset.db).\n\nBehavioral requirements:\n- Preserve previous functionality and error messages for attribute where input validation.\n- Support filtering by slug/name equality/options, numeric ranges/equality/oneOf, boolean equality, date and datetime ranges, and reference attributes with containsAll/containsAny for pages, products, variants, and global IDs.\n- Use the queryset’s db alias (qs.db) for all Attribute/AttributeValue/assigned model queries.\n- The shared functions must be reusable by other entity types by passing their assigned attribute model and foreign key field name.",
-      "prompt": "Consolidate attribute filtering and validation into a shared attribute GraphQL module and update page filters to use it. Create generic helpers to build filtering expressions for attribute values (slug/name, numeric, boolean, date, datetime, and reference lists) that work with any entity by accepting the assigned attribute model and its foreign key field name. Validate the attribute where input consistently (no duplicate slugs, non-empty value with a single key, type-specific keys matching the attribute input type, and proper reference containsAll/containsAny semantics) and raise the same errors. Update the page where filter to import these helpers, delegate attribute filtering to the shared function, and call the shared validator in is_valid. Ensure all DB queries use the queryset’s db alias and that the refactor preserves existing behavior and results for attribute-based queries.",
