-      "spec": "Implement dedicated, normalized storage for Adyen-specific transaction attributes and route them through the gateway response and persistence layer.\n\nScope and required changes:\n\n1) Data contract: saleor/payment/interface.py\n- In the GatewayResponse dataclass, add two optional string fields:\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method\n- Keep raw_response but annotate with a deprecation comment indicating it is deprecated.\n\n2) Persistence model: saleor/payment/models.py\n- In the Transaction model, add two nullable TextField columns:\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code = models.TextField(null=True)\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method = models.TextField(null=True)\n- Add a model docstring/comment explaining these are temporary Adyen-only fields to support removing gateway_response later.\n- Leave gateway_response as-is (JSONField) but mark it as deprecated via a comment.\n\n3) Database migrations (new files):\n- saleor/payment/migrations/0061_transaction_legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method_and_more.py\n  - Migration that adds the two new fields to the payment_transaction table (Transaction model).\n- saleor/payment/migrations/0064_merge_20250716_0709.py\n  - Merge migration that depends on 0061 above and an existing 0063 to resolve migration graph (use your repo’s latest numbers if they differ).\n\n4) Transaction creation: saleor/payment/utils.py\n- In create_transaction(), when constructing the Transaction instance, pass through the two new fields from the provided GatewayResponse to the Transaction model fields.\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code=gateway_response.legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method=gateway_response.legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method\n\n5) Adyen plugin behavior: saleor/payment/gateways/adyen/plugin.py\n- Import logging and define logger = logging.getLogger(__name__).\n- Add a helper method _normalize_response_field(field: str) -> str that returns field.strip().lower().\n- Replace direct result.message[\"resultCode\"].strip().lower() usages with self._normalize_response_field(result.message[\"resultCode\"]).\n- When creating GatewayResponse instances in these methods, populate the two new fields with normalized values (using the helper):\n  - process_payment()\n  - _process_additional_action()\n  - confirm_payment() (the return path that builds GatewayResponse from existing transaction)\n  - refund_payment()\n  - capture_payment()\n  - void_payment()\n  Set:\n    legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method = normalized paymentMethod value from the Adyen response (default empty string if missing)\n    legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code = normalized resultCode value from the Adyen response (default empty string if missing)\n  Keep raw_response assigned to the raw Adyen response and annotate with a deprecation comment.\n- In confirm_payment():\n  - Read result_code from transaction.legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code if present; otherwise fallback to normalized transaction.gateway_response[\"resultCode\"].\n  - Read payment_method from transaction.legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method if present; otherwise fallback to normalized transaction.gateway_response[\"paymentMethod\"].\n  - If both legacy fields are missing (i.e., both reads fell back), log a warning: \"Reading deprecated raw_response from Adyen plugin.\". Maintain existing logic around PENDING_STATUSES and AUTH_STATUS with iDEAL.\n\n6) Adyen webhooks: saleor/payment/gateways/adyen/webhooks.py\n- When creating GatewayResponse for create_new_transaction() and handle_api_response():\n  - Populate legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method and legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code with normalized (strip + lower) values derived from notification/response structures.\n  - Keep raw_response as before and annotate with a deprecation comment.\n\n7) Tests: saleor/payment/gateways/adyen/tests/test_plugin.py\n- Update tests that create/compare expected GatewayResponse values to include the two new fields. For example, in test_process_additional_action expected GatewayResponse should include:\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_result_code set to normalized resultCode\n  - legacy_adyen_plugin_payment_method set to normalized paymentMethod (empty string when not provided)\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- All Adyen plugin and webhook-created GatewayResponse objects include the two legacy_adyen_plugin_* fields with normalized strings.\n- Transaction records created from those responses persist these values in the new Transaction columns.\n- confirm_payment() uses the new Transaction fields primarily, with a logged warning when falling back to deprecated gateway_response, and behavior remains consistent with previous logic.\n- Database migrations apply cleanly and tests pass.\n",
-      "prompt": "Enhance the Adyen payment integration to stop relying on the generic raw gateway response JSON for core decision-making. Add explicit, normalized fields for the Adyen result code and payment method, persist them on transactions, and use them during confirmation. Update the gateway response contract and webhooks to carry these values through, keep backward compatibility with a clear deprecation warning when falling back to the raw response, and add migrations and tests accordingly.",
